# Fantasy performance

- Prefer materialized caches over live `predict_*` on hub routes: `artifacts/draft_pool/`, `artifacts/weekly_predictions/`.
- Pool vs overlay: `build_draft_pool_payload()` then `build_value_overlay()` in `value_sheet.py`. Do not recompute the pool per request.
- Roster/cap reads are DB-only. Sleeper runs on link/sync, or `GET /api/hub/roster?live_sleeper=1` for a one-off pull.
- `GET /api/hub/home` and `GET /league/{id}/freshness` serve the last-known snapshot (`stale_as_of`) and never parse commissioner workbooks or block on Sleeper. Cap-sheet stale uses file mtimes vs stored `file_fingerprint`. Workbook parse stays on explicit sheet sync.
- Hub `GET /media/{id}` serves the original unless `?w=` is set. Snap to 48 / 96 / 256, cache the WebP variant next to the file, and never resize on a cache hit. Clients request the painted size — do not ship the studio original for a 22px mark.
- Scoring history lives in SQLite `sleeper_scoring_cache`. Refresh on league sync or `GET /api/hub/league/{id}/insights?refresh=1`.
- CPU-heavy work uses `app/process_pool.py`. Do not start a per-route process pool.
- Secrets and paths go through `src/config.py`, not raw `os.environ` in routes.
- `HUB_TIMING=true` logs slow hub routes (>500ms) and may set `X-Hub-Timing-MS`.
- After mlready or model changes, rebuild the draft pool with `preseason_refresh`. `scripts/ops/fix_artifact_fingerprints.py` only audits saved data; never relabel an old forecast as current. Do not leave first-visit Fantasy pages on cold live inference.

## Measurement and perceived speed

Perceived speed follows the same architecture: paint roster/cap snapshots first, retain known content during refresh, reserve image/skeleton geometry, and make selection/previews immediate. Trades loads Ideas/Inbox on demand and reuses the existing account/league/team-scoped weekly snapshot. Measure cold/warm navigation and a representative interaction before claiming an improvement; record device/viewport, cache state, and data source.

Future field-measurement targets are LCP ≤2.5s, INP ≤200ms, and CLS ≤0.1 at the 75th percentile, segmented by phone/desktop ([Core Web Vitals thresholds](https://web.dev/articles/defining-core-web-vitals-thresholds)). These are targets, not current results; one local lab render cannot establish a field percentile. Do not add a telemetry dependency or more polling just to populate the rollout log.
